<title>INDIA: Modest world rally boosts Indian gold rates.</title>
<headline>Modest world rally boosts Indian gold rates.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-02-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indian gold and silver prices showed gains in early trade on Tuesday, dealers said.</p>
<p>Renewed seasonal buying at reduced levels as well as low arrivals sent up prices, they said. On Monday gold was down by 15 rupees per 10 grammes and silver was down by 10 rupees per kg.</p>
<p>&quot;Reports of a modest rally in the world market also prompted some speculative interest in local markets,&quot; one dealer said.</p>
<p>Prices of a gold biscuit (116.50 grammes) rose in mid-morning trade on Tuesday by 200 rupees to 56,600 rupees.  </p>
